# Customer app (Tokajo)

## Scope
- Work **only** inside `coustmer/`. Do not edit other apps, services, or folders unless the user explicitly names them.
- Treat anything outside `coustmer/` as out of scope.

## Git (every prompt)
- After finishing the prompt, **commit** relevant `coustmer/` changes (and this rule if it changed).
- **Do not push** unless the user explicitly asks.
- Follow the existing commit safety protocol: no force push, no `--no-verify`, no amending unless allowed.
- Skip empty commits. Do not commit secrets (`.env`, keys, credentials).

## Product bar
- UX and flows should feel like **Swiggy / Zomato**: fast home, category → dishes, restaurant menu, cart, COD/online pay, tracking.
- Code must be **production-ready**: typed, no dummy/seed fallbacks in user paths, real API wiring, loading/empty/error states, no leftover debug, no broken JSX.
- Prefer one clear API call over N+1. Match list/detail/filter APIs to the UI. Keep navigation deep-links working (category → item → restaurant menu).

## Everything must work
- Do not leave a task half-done. Features, APIs, screens, and taps must work end-to-end before you stop.
- Verify routes match (no unmatched screens), payloads match the backend, filters show the right items, and loading/error/empty states are real.
- Fix syntax/lint/runtime issues you introduce. Do not ship broken JSX, dead buttons, or fake success.
- If something cannot work yet (missing backend), say so clearly — do not paper over it with dummy data.
